-cdf69250-d5d3-48f8-b67d-2a10f2578856"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d3c5f059f2c883a2a27096ed4bb463213e8853fd2af1affb56c52c4616b7ad5a","event_uuid":"406b7823-7064-4d96-8539-34904fee81e8","position":{"commit_sha":"dbe296ebb36f0528e7410b4f5ae3fb1467033047","position":"1787522425592021001-406b7823-7064-4d96-8539-34904fee81e8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"93766bc5bd97706e8c50ff586d4004f0487c56563fe211e70857ae691bf64e94","event_uuid":"c37efdc0-c899-4d1c-a118-d035036783cf","position":{"commit_sha":"f814b147060b4b416f1c8d1f486bb844db37438a","position":"1787522766528292001-c37efdc0-c899-4d1c-a118-d035036783cf"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"dc74ee0f7bba4e31b9c646582d7ec9992476ed40ecc95437bdfb6f869ced2f03","event_uuid":"c7402e37-5212-4323-95e7-aff36386cd2d","position":{"commit_sha":"a67ba5415822686e6c0c718968ab93825b6f41bc","position":"1787522788935307001-c7402e37-5212-4323-95e7-aff36386cd2d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"FORCE_CLOSE: close gate(s) bypassed by user approval — no completion/signature attestation was signed. Reason: \"Gerrit change 2104 both gates green (LLM-Review+1 PASS, Verified+1 SUCCESS) and MERGED to main as 98c428ec42; file_impact updated to the 4 actually-merged files\". Session: 98c428ec42.","timestamp":1787400197206365001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787290343130188001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6b83f9e8-9d2c-4f89-a5c8-a6fae49b21da","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"bfe7-0900-c3d1-4141"},{"link_uuid":"b8c25fc7-4e26-45e8-9621-f88bf7e2b88d","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"ad81-73ad-83bb-47c7"},{"link_uuid":"38796822-a2d9-4a69-b0c2-f3a00ee81921","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f8e7-aeca-a4e4-4e12"},{"link_uuid":"aacf41a0-37fa-403c-ad45-615d8bd149f6","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2e2d-9de4-ab16-4854"},{"link_uuid":"df72fc98-8d5a-45d6-98bf-dca677afac46","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"a9ab-57fe-3089-4975"}],"description":"# Doctor: mapping-config diagnostics with offline-always / live-drift-degrades portability\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nThe mapping seam (S1–S8) adds a hand-editable `[mapping]` config surface. Two failure classes\nneed surfacing before a reconcile silently drifts:\n\n- **Internally-invalid config** — already fail-closed via `MappingConfigError`: a non-integer\n  `hierarchy` / malformed block fail at LOAD; out-of-vocabulary and unmapped-non-skipped values\n  fail in the `config` resolvers. Doctor surfaces these as **error** findings.\n- **Live drift** — internally valid but disagreeing with live Jira (a mapped status/type/link\n  Jira dropped). Surface when Jira is reachable; degrade cleanly when not.\n\n`rebar doctor` is the existing diagnostic home, so extend it. It must stay portable: it runs\nwhere the optional **`jira-datacenter`** extra is absent and no credentials are set — offline\nchecks always run; the live-drift check degrades to an `unavailable` finding, mirroring\n`rebar metrics` (`docs/user-guide.md`).\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a mapping-diagnostics function to `src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py`, wired into `scan`.\nMapping findings go in their **own list** (as for scan-dirty/lock reports), are rendered and\nfolded into the exit code, and kept **out of** `run_repair`'s iteration — so `doctor.scan()`'s\nblocking-edge finding contract (and `tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor.py`) is unchanged.\n\n- **Offline checks (always run, stdlib-only, no Jira import):** first call\n  `mapping_config.load_mapping_config` inside `try/except MappingConfigError` — a load-time\n  failure (non-integer hierarchy, or a malformed axis/vocabulary block) becomes one **error**\n  finding whose `detail` is the `MappingConfigError` message verbatim — it already frames the key\n  in either prefix format (`[mapping.<where>]:` for axis/hierarchy/layer, `[mapping].<where>:`\n  for vocabulary), so no brittle parsing — and the per-key pass is skipped. On a successful load, enumerate `config.projects` **union the default layer** and, per\n  key, run the provider-neutral `config` resolvers — `effective_status_map`, `effective_type_map`,\n  `assert_type_decisions_complete`, `effective_link_map` — which inject the built-in\n  `MappingLayer` + `Capability`, import `mapping_config` lazily, and are stdlib-only at import\n  (never `adapters.jira*`); a resolve-time `MappingConfigError` (out-of-vocabulary,\n  unmapped-non-skipped) → an **error** finding naming the key (non-zero exit). On the same per-key pass, one genuinely *soft* problem — an all-empty `projects.<KEY>` block\n  (likely a stub) — is a **warning** naming the key, not an error.\n- **Live-drift check (best-effort, degrades):** run only when the `jira-datacenter` extra is\n  importable — gated through `rebar._optional.capability_installed(\"jira_datacenter\")` — AND\n  credentials resolve. On the available path, reuse S8's read-only probe reader\n  (`mapping_probe.build_probe`) and diff configured vs observed vocabulary, one finding per\n  divergence on the axes the reader observes — **status, type, link** (a configured value absent\n  from Jira's set).\n  Hierarchy is deliberately **excluded** from the live diff: `build_probe` resolves Data Center,\n  where `mapping_probe._hierarchy` is always empty (`hierarchyLevel` is Cloud-only) — so a\n  hierarchy divergence is structurally undetectable here (offline hierarchy validity still\n  covered above). When the\n  extra is absent, OR the resolved PAT is empty (`JIRA_PAT` unset — `resolve_jira_datacenter_settings`\n  returns `pat=\"\"`), OR settings resolution raises `ConfigError` (fail-loud on a malformed\n  `[tool.rebar.reconciler]`), OR the probe\n  transport raises or times out (the probe call runs under a doctor-side bounded wall-clock\n  timeout — a daemon worker thread with `result(timeout=…)`, bound a module constant (default\n  10s), since S8's `build_client_from_settings` sets none; a timed-out thread is abandoned and\n  doctor returns promptly with `unavailable`), emit a single `unavailable` finding\n  (\"live mapping-drift check skipped: <reason>\") and return success — never raise. The Jira import\n  and probe construction happen lazily behind the guard, wrapped so every degradation cause\n  folds into the one `unavailable` finding.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py` — new mapping-diagnostics function (own findings list); the\n  `capability_installed(\"jira_datacenter\")` guard and lazy Jira import.\n- `docs/user-guide.md` — document the offline error/warning findings and the `unavailable`\n  live-drift convention.\n- Reuses S1's `mapping_config` (via `config` resolvers) and S8's `mapping_probe.build_probe`.\n- Out of scope: `--repair` for mapping config (report-only); Jira as a hard doctor dependency;\n  the live-drift **true path against real Jira** — transport is S8's proven read-only probe\n  reader (covered by S8), so this child proves the diff logic via an injected vocabulary and\n  treats the real-transport path as not-applicable.\n\n## Testing\n\n- **Unit (offline tier), no Jira import:** temp config with (a) valid mapping → no findings;\n  (b) each error-class problem — a load-time one in each message format (non-integer hierarchy\n  `[mapping.<where>]:`, and a malformed vocabulary list `[mapping].<where>:`) and a resolve-time\n  one (out-of-vocabulary value, unmapped-non-skipped type) → an **error** finding whose detail\n  carries the key + non-zero exit; (c) an all-empty `projects.<KEY>` block → a **warning**. Asserts\n  no `adapters.jira` import on this path. Oracle: finding list + exit code.\n- **Unit (portability tier):** force the guard false (monkeypatch `capability_installed` for\n  `\"jira_datacenter\"`) → exactly one `unavailable` finding, success exit, no Jira import. Oracle:\n  the single finding + zero exit.\n- **Unit (degradation causes):** guard true; drive each cause — empty resolved PAT, a\n  `ConfigError` from settings resolution, and a slow/hanging probe reader exceeding the\n  doctor-side timeout — each folds into one `unavailable` finding with the matching reason +\n  success exit. Oracle: the finding + reason + zero exit.\n- **Unit (live-drift tier), injected transport:** inject a fake probe reader whose vocabulary\n  diverges on status, type, and link → one drift finding per divergence naming the axis + absent\n  value. No live Jira. Oracle: the per-axis finding set.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `rebar doctor` on a valid `[mapping]` config with the `jira-datacenter` extra absent\n  succeeds and emits exactly one `unavailable` live-drift finding — portability-tier test (guard\n  forced false via `capability_installed`, no Jira import, zero exit).\n- [x] Each offline error-class problem yields an **error** finding whose detail carries the key\n  + non-zero exit: both load-error message formats (non-integer hierarchy `[mapping.<where>]:`\n  and malformed vocabulary `[mapping].<where>:`) surfaced verbatim, plus the resolve-time errors\n  (out-of-vocabulary value, unmapped-non-skipped type) reached by enumerating `config.projects`\n  + the default layer per key — offline-tier test asserting the `MappingConfigError`-derived\n  finding.\n- [x] An all-empty `projects.<KEY>` stub yields a **warning** finding naming the key (not an\n  error, not a non-zero exit) — offline-tier test.\n- [x] Each degradation cause — extra absent, empty resolved PAT (`JIRA_PAT` unset), a\n  `ConfigError` from settings resolution, and a slow/hanging probe exceeding the doctor-side\n  timeout — folds into a single `unavailable` finding + reason + success exit — portability and\n  degradation-cause tests.\n- [x] With a fake probe reader injected, each configured-vs-observed divergence on status, type,\n  and link yields a drift finding naming the axis + absent value — live-drift-tier test.\n  Hierarchy is excluded by design (the reused Data Center probe never observes `hierarchyLevel`).\n- [x] `docs/user-guide.md` documents the new mapping diagnostics.\n\nAll four tiers run in-process, no live Jira, no specific CI provider — satisfying\n`project.portability`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/doctor_mapping.py","reason":"new module: offline + live-drift mapping diagnostics with engine-path bootstrap"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py","reason":"wire mapping findings into doctor_cli, JSON, text, exit-code fold"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_doctor_mapping.py","reason":"held-out oracle: 13 tests across offline/stub/portability/degradation/drift/exit tiers"},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"document mapping diagnostics + unavailable convention"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","force_close_reason":"Gerrit change 2104 both gates green (LLM-Review+1 PASS, Verified+1 SUCCESS) and MERGED to main as 98c428ec42; file_impact updated to the 4 actually-merged files","keyring":[],"last_reopened_at":1787521499527498001,"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","ad81-73ad-83bb-47c7"],["depends_on","bfe7-0900-c3d1-4141"],["parent","3d7a-7795-efde-4df7"],["relates_to","2e2d-9de4-ab16-4854"],["relates_to","a9ab-57fe-3089-4975"],["relates_to","f8e7-aeca-a4e4-4e12"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"3d7a-7795-efde-4df7","parent_status_uuid":"c37efdc0-c899-4d1c-a118-d035036783cf","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"52b0-6a6a-c66b-4c59","ticket_type":"story","title":"Doctor: mapping-config diagnostics with offline-always / live-drift-degrades portability","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["df72fc98-8d5a-45d6-98bf-dca677afac46","22359979-4302-4d6e-99e6-9616316d1255","33f4ab45-d0d6-48ba-a76b-31224ac3098a","1baa874a-6aaf-4c20-b17c-cd1a25ce5067","f79f0d1e-eb8c-4fce-b2ca-ea902b60bf6a","8dcedb71-2e62-4166-b7e9-55c92f6dc28c","3040046e-843b-41ce-a0ae-80d78c7b5b4b","cdf69250-d5d3-48f8-b67d-2a10f2578856","406b7823-7064-4d96-8539-34904fee81e8","c37efdc0-c899-4d1c-a118-d035036783cf","c7402e37-5212-4323-95e7-aff36386cd2d"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787548146698676001,"uuid":"0941e464-8314-407d-b40c-4de9a961f8d3"}